type: software
title: "Extremal laws for coupon collection with group drawings"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. A collector draws random packages of s out of n coupons. When the omitted coupons can form a Steiner 2-design, sampling it is the slowest fair law at every number of draws. In every critical window n p^k -> lambda the slowest fair mean is k + min(1, lambda) + o(1), against k + 1 - e^(-lambda) for uniform sampling. No fair law is more than 1/e + (1 - gamma)/ln(n/r) draws slower on average than uniform sampling, with the limit 1/e attained. An exhaustive exact search covers all small cases. On the fast side, every law has mean at least max{x H_x, 1 + x} with x = n/s, proving the Fang-Chang conjecture with uniqueness."
